Package: HSMap
Type: Package
Title: Maternal Linkage Mapping in Open-Pollinated Diploid Families
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: c(
    person("Marcelo", "Mollinari", email = "mmollina@gmail.com",
           role = c("aut", "cre")),
    person("Kim", "McKeever", role = "aut"),
    person("Molly", "Irvin", role = "aut"),
    person("Fikret", "Isik", role = "aut")
  )
Description: A fast C++ (Rcpp) maternal hidden Markov model for building maternal
             linkage maps in open-pollinated (unknown-sire) diploid half-sib families.
             For a single family, the unknown paternal contribution is integrated out
             through a per-marker paternal gametic frequency estimated jointly with the
             recombination map; maps are fitted within resolved phase blocks, and
             no-linkage intervals are reported as gaps rather than large centimorgan
             distances. Extensions that pool several dams under one shared map (via a
             joint EM) and that handle known-sire full-sib crosses are included and
             documented as forthcoming.
